translated_text:
Article 33

The Regional Government, in preventing acts of violence against women:
a. carries out the preparation and dissemination of information regarding matters related to violence against women;
b. carries out dissemination regarding the rights of Women;
c. seeks to improve education for Women;
d. opens skills courses for Women to support the economic needs of the family;
e. creates employment opportunities for Women;
f. provides counseling related to Violence Against Women;
g. empowers social community organizations and Women's organizations at the Regional, sub-district, and village levels to increase the knowledge and insight of Women;
h. establishes complaint posts for the Protection of Women; and
i. forms a network in efforts to prevent Violence Against Women.

